course: dictionary
lesson: 15000
title: A word for what is needed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Requisite» is a long, formal word for something that is needed for a purpose. Look at the clues around it. If a recipe needs the requisite eggs, it needs the eggs that are necessary, so the cake can be made.
explain: «You need the requisite number of votes to win.» The clues are votes and win. Try your meaning in the sentence: "You need the needed number of votes to win." It still makes sense, so requisite means needed.
explain: Requisite can also be a noun, a thing that is needed. «Soap and toothpaste are toilet requisites.» Shops use the word for things people need for a purpose. A prerequisite is something needed first, before you can do something else.
fact: Requisite is an adjective meaning needed for a purpose, or necessary.
fact: As a noun, a requisite is a thing that is needed. Its plural is requisites.
fact: «The requisite amount» means the amount that is needed.
fact: «Toilet requisites» are things like soap and toothpaste.
fact: A prerequisite is something needed first, before something else can happen.
exercise: «You must have the requisite skills to join the team.» What does requisite mean here? | Broken | *Needed | Very loud | Funny
exercise: The shop sells toilet requisites. What are these? | Old toilets from a museum | Games for the bath | Big signs for the door | *Things like soap and toothpaste that people need
exercise: «A prerequisite for the course is basic maths.» What does prerequisite mean? | Something you can skip | Something very cold | A type of prize | *Something needed first
test: «She had all the requisite ingredients for the cake.» What does requisite mean? | *Needed | Burnt | Frozen | Sweet
test: A requisite is a thing that is needed. What is the plural of requisite? | *requisites | requisitor | requisitee | requisiteses
exam: Which sentence uses requisite as a noun, meaning a thing that is needed? | The requisite amount of flour is two cups. | *Soap and toothpaste are toilet requisites. | You need the requisite number of votes. | She has the requisite skills for the job.
